{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>From the dew of the heavens.</b> The blessing is not that Elohim will give him the dew of the heavens, for dew descends everywhere; and if He had said that He would give an abundance of dew or that it would fall in its proper season, as in the sense of \"and I will give your rains in their season\" (Leviticus 26:4), that would be a blessing. Rather, its meaning is that He mentioned in it the blessing of YHWH like the fragrance of the field that YHWH has blessed — and the sense of \"that Elohim has blessed\" to my son is that HaShem blessed him in the field, meaning that He would grant him success there in his hunting, and that he would not die and no evil would befall him there. And He said, <b>\"And may Elohim give you of the dew of the heavens and of the fatness of the earth,\"</b> and the blessing is the addition and abundance, or that \"and abundance of grain and wine\" comes as an addition with the vav, and its measurement is: \"And may Elohim give you of the dew of the heavens and of the fatness of the earth — abundance of grain and wine.\" And the correct interpretation in my eyes is that the gift of Elohim is constant and never ceases forever; therefore He said, \"And may Elohim give you all your days upon your land the dew of the heavens,\" and He will give you of the fatness of the earth, meaning its fatness in all lands, as in the sense of what is written (Ezekiel 20:6), \"it is the splendor of all the lands.\" And Rabbi Abraham said (Ibn Ezra on Genesis 27:28) that the mem of מִטַּל (\"of the dew\") draws the noun itself along with something else with it, that is, מִן מִשְּׁמַנֵּי הָאָרֶץ (\"of the fatness of the earth\"). And to Esau, nothing was given as a gift of Elohim nor in abundance; rather, He said, \"But you too I have assigned after him, and the fatness of the earth and the dew of the heavens shall be your dwelling\" — while you dwell there, hinting that it will be consumed and lost, but while it lasts, his portion will be good."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:35:55.296018292Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}